FreeType 2.14 changed FT_Outline::tags from 'char*' to 'unsigned char*'
(and n_points / n_contours / contours from signed to unsigned short),
which makes the initialisation below ill-formed:

  error: cannot initialize a variable of type 'const char *'
         with an rvalue of type 'unsigned char *'

OCE 0.18.3 predates that change and upstream (tpaviot/oce) is archived,
so fix it here. An explicit cast is used rather than retyping aTags so
that the patch stays valid against both pre- and post-2.14 FreeType
headers; FT_CURVE_TAG() masks with 0x03, so signedness is irrelevant to
every use of aTags below.

diff --git src/Font/Font_BRepFont.cxx src/Font/Font_BRepFont.cxx
--- src/Font/Font_BRepFont.cxx
+++ src/Font/Font_BRepFont.cxx
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@
   for (short aContour = 0, aStartIndex = 0; aContour < anOutline.n_contours; ++aContour)
   {
     const FT_Vector* aPntList = &anOutline.points[aStartIndex];
-    const char* aTags      = &anOutline.tags[aStartIndex];
+    const char* aTags      = (const char* )&anOutline.tags[aStartIndex];
     const short anEndIndex = anOutline.contours[aContour];
     const short aPntsNb    = (anEndIndex - aStartIndex) + 1;
     aStartIndex = anEndIndex + 1;
